# On WSO2 Agent Manager: attach an LLM provider to the agent in the console. The platform injects its
# gateway URL and key (default names <AGENT>_1_URL / <AGENT>_1_API_KEY), and the agent picks them up.
# You don't need an OpenAI key there. To name them explicitly, rename them in the console to:
# LLM_PROVIDER_URL=https://<gateway>/<path>
# LLM_PROVIDER_KEY=<platform-issued key>
# LLM_PROVIDER_AUTH_HEADER=API-Key     # only if the provider's Security header name is different

# Local development without the platform: your own OpenAI key
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o

# Optional
# AGENT_PORT=8000
# DEMO_TODAY=2026-09-28                # pin the date the assistant sees
